  "changes": [
    "Independent recovery and handoff pages now list physical retained history in 20-record pages and offer original preview, explicit archive confirmation, original query and explicit same-ID metadata continuation",
    "Cold restore/start archives require the original encrypted backup and passphrase with original fingerprint verification; handoff archives retain the original grant/token binding; grant-scoped listings cannot expose a foreign grant",
    "Review DTOs expose bounded identifiers/state/permission flags only; confirmation digest binds private original bytes, Root proof, namespace/data identity and saved local intent; stale confirmation never dispatches",
    "Saved metadata IDs remain original; missing Root originals and lost HTTP replies are query-only, never late first sends; only an affirmative matching original Root metadata intent permits explicit metadata continuation",
    "Browser material stays in memory and is cleared on submit/cancel/page lifecycle changes; delayed previews cannot restore write permission after lifecycle invalidation; native dialog and native validation retain keyboard behavior",
    "New archive.js is a separately attested static asset; recovery.js remains byte-for-byte unchanged. Each asset retains the 65536-byte bound; helper source limit remains 131072",
    "Exact old three-static-asset JOURNAL_V1 profile remains supported alongside the new four-static-asset profile. Both still create positive package-history/startup handoffs; UNKNOWN blocks before mutating systemd actions"
  ],
